.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt VOP_RENAME 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm VOP_RENAME
.Nd rename a file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.In sys/fcntl.h
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_RENAME "struct vnode *fdvp" "struct vnode *fvp" "struct componentname *fcnp" "struct vnode *tdvp" "struct vnode *tvp" "struct componentname *tcnp" "u_int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This renames a file and possibly changes its parent directory.
Unless an exchange is requested, an existing destination object is removed.
.Pp
Its arguments are:
.Bl -tag -width fdvp
.It Fa fdvp
The vnode of the old parent directory.
.It Fa fvp
The vnode of the file to be renamed.
.It Fa fcnp
Pathname information about the file's current name.
.It Fa tdvp
The vnode of the new parent directory.
.It Fa tvp
The vnode of the target file (if it exists).
.It Fa tcnp
Pathname information about the file's new name.
.It Fa flags
Zero or one of
.Dv AT_RENAME_NOREPLACE
and
.Dv AT_RENAME_EXCHANGE .
The first rejects an existing destination.
The second atomically exchanges two existing directory entries; the objects
may have different types and directories need not be empty.
Unsupported flags must be rejected with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
before any modification.
.El
.Pp
Filesystems implementing exchange must authorize both directions.
After acquiring locks on the final four vnodes, call
.Fn vn_rename_exchange_check
with the six vnode and component-name arguments before modifying either entry.
This checks native MAC permissions; the filesystem must also enforce
its native access, immutability, and directory-cycle checks in both directions.
ABI sandbox checks apply to the accessed VFS path, which can have different
ancestry from the underlying filesystem path.
For either ordinary rename or exchange, if relocking changes an object, return
.Er ERELOOKUP
so the VFS can repeat lookup, recheck permissions on the accessed path,
and retain the correct objects for notifications.
The objects and parent directories must be in vnode sequence-counter write
sections while changing the entries and updating the name cache with
.Fn cache_vop_exchange .
.Sh LOCKS
The source directory and file are unlocked but are expected to have their
ref count bumped on entry.
The VOP routine is expected to
.Xr vrele 9
both prior
to returning.
.Pp
The destination directory and file are locked as well as having their ref
count bumped.
The VOP routine is expected to
.Xr vput 9
both prior to
returning.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EPERM
The file is immutable.
.It Bq Er EXDEV
It is not possible to rename a file between different file systems.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An attempt was made to rename
.Pa \&.
or
.Pa .. ,
or to perform an operation which would break the directory tree structure.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support the requested flags.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
An exchange was requested and either directory entry is missing.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
An ordinary rename attempted to replace a directory with a file or vice versa.
.It Bq Er ENOTEMPTY
An attempt was made to remove a directory which is not empty.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9
.Sh AUTHORS
This manual page was written by
.An Doug Rabson .
